Package: grist
Title: Mergeable Sufficient Statistics on S2 Cells from Daily Grids
Version: 0.0.2
Authors@R: person("Michael", "Sumner", email = "mdsumner@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: The engine extracted from trend.sst: area-weighted daily
    grids accumulated to a global S2 discrete grid as sufficient
    statistics (count, summed weights, weighted sums and sums of
    squares), one Parquet file per date. A source is a catalog of
    dates plus a grid signature; a region is a cell selection; every
    mean, variance, or rollup is exact arithmetic on the sums. Catalog
    rows are classic (one band of a file) or multidimensional (an array
    sliced by coordinate value), on geographic or projected grids.
    Deployments (product knowledge, catalogs, schedules, sites) live in
    host repositories; this package is the invariant middle.
